  "confidence": "medium",
  "notes": "ROS 1 package; all ten packet elements are provided API symbols (XML tags, an expression constant, two executables, a namespace prefix). No .msg/.srv/.action definitions exist, so msg_type, units, QoS (ROS 1), rates and definition_id are null; frame is 'none' because none of these carry spatial data. The package ships two processors: src/xacro/__init__.py (legacy; used by scripts/xacro and xacro.py unless '--inorder' is in argv, scripts/xacro:48-55, xacro.py:55-62) and src/xacro_jade/__init__.py (in-order). declares cites the legacy module for the tags; the in-order counterparts are xacro_jade:791 (insert_block), :568/:815 (property), :344 (include), :522/:819 (macro). In xacro_jade, non-prefixed tags (<property>, <insert_block>, <macro>, <include>) are accepted with a deprecation warning only while xacro_ns is True (default), and rejected under --xacro-ns (xacro_jade:151-167, cli.py:78-79); the legacy module accepts them unconditionally (plain <include> with element children is ignored, legacy :230-242). api:pi is declared only in xacro_jade (line 114, via math.__dict__); the legacy module defines no pi (eval_lit looks symbols up only in the property Table, legacy :360-386). api:xmlns:xacro: no code checks the namespace URI; tags are matched by the literal 'xacro:' prefix. The URI http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro appears only in the parse-error hint (legacy :681, xacro_jade :1009); the legacy include step copies xmlns:* attributes of included documents to the root (legacy :278-291). api:xacro is taken as the installed executable (CMakeLists.txt:17); the Python packages xacro and xacro_jade are also installed (setup.py:7). exclusive is empty: no hardware or device handles. references lists cross-package symbols the code calls (roslaunch substitution_args, rosgraph.names, rospkg). test/test_inorder_with_invalid_include.xml is present but not referenced by test/test_xacro.py, which tests only the legacy module."
